WEBVTT

NOTE Narrated by a synthetic voice (an ElevenLabs stock voice); the opening disclosure is the macOS Trinoids voice. Text by Phil Renato.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.198
TitersTrinitiesTruth (Monte Carlo mythophilioma)

00:00:07.198 --> 00:00:12.556
Today, I saw a Nazi driving a lowered, silver BMW with chrome-tinted windows.

00:00:12.556 --> 00:00:17.915
The bumper of the 740i had a single sticker on it—a blue rectangle with three

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:23.132
yellow, left-pointing arrows. He was maintaining the speed limit, making it

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:28.631
difficult to make out the particular gold basketweave BBS wheel type, but I was

00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:34.272
pretty sure they were style 5S. There was a blip of red on each rim as it rolled,

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:39.771
which I took for some kind of sticker. It could have been some driftcar-related

00:00:39.771 --> 00:00:45.482
overbranding, but it also could have been a swastika. Even in West Michigan, overt

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:50.487
fundamentalist fascism is generally frowned upon. This is a very polite,

00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:55.352
conservative community; people mumble-pray at McDonald’s before eating

00:00:55.352 --> 00:01:00.922
their cowflesh McMuffins—even when they are by themselves. As the BMW passed me,

00:01:00.922 --> 00:01:06.492
I wondered how difficult it might be to unmask its drivers, to get them to admit

00:01:06.492 --> 00:01:11.921
not just what they think, but to study how they came to these ideas. (Did they

00:01:11.921 --> 00:01:16.997
choose them as adults, or were they bred into them at the dinner table?).

00:01:16.997 --> 00:01:22.461
This American Life was running a story about another conservative zealot, one

00:01:22.461 --> 00:01:27.997
who had proudly confessed to his crimes. On Nov 4, 1995, Prime Minister Yitzak

00:01:27.997 --> 00:01:33.462
Rabin was walking down a set of stairs to get into his car after a successful

00:01:33.462 --> 00:01:38.998
political rally in Israel, when he was shot twice in the back by Yigal Amir, a

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:44.893
25 year old Israeli Tea Party Patriot. In the two decades since, the Israeli public

00:01:44.893 --> 00:01:50.789
have been driven rightward, and a whisper of conspiracy has grown into iron myth by

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:56.109
the very people Amir gave voice to. “It’s the prerogative of the conspiracy

00:01:56.109 --> 00:02:00.927
theorists to never have to answer questions, just to raise them” the

00:02:00.927 --> 00:02:06.822
narrator opined. The license plate on the 740i read PANZ3R, and as I turned onto my

00:02:06.822 --> 00:02:12.358
street I started thinking about how many Germans thought that their tanks were

00:02:12.358 --> 00:02:18.038
loaded with blanks—that the entire war was slipped into memory by sneaky British

00:02:18.038 --> 00:02:18.901
pickpockets?

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:24.602
We are what we wear, what books we own, what cars we drive; interconnected bits

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:30.522
of information, dissolving in atmosphere. We know and remember the things we touch

00:02:30.522 --> 00:02:36.149
and smell together, the things we hear that happen to match up with the things

00:02:36.149 --> 00:02:41.192
we read. We are masters of our domain every time we recognize that our

00:02:41.192 --> 00:02:46.893
ambitions, and skills, and industries are extinguished as they crash into flaw.

00:02:46.893 --> 00:02:50.109
Some failures are crimes, but others, virtue.

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:55.123
When Siegfried Knemeyer was escaping Berlin, he ditched his BMW as he

00:02:55.123 --> 00:03:00.873
approached a group of British soldiers. He would eventually be captured, hiding

00:03:00.873 --> 00:03:06.329
under a nearby bridge. This lack of Nazi-corporate-car strategy spared him,

00:03:06.329 --> 00:03:11.711
at least immediately, from being recognized for the senior officer that he

00:03:11.711 --> 00:03:16.872
was. After a brief imprisonment, he returned to Germany, worked for the

00:03:16.872 --> 00:03:22.107
French, and then for the US Air Force. “Dynamic Max” went from being the

00:03:22.107 --> 00:03:27.563
commander-in-chief of the Luftwaffe and technical adviser to Hermann Goring

00:03:27.563 --> 00:03:33.019
(where he planned to bomb New York City with radioactive sand) to being the

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:38.622
technical director of Wright Field in Dayton—helping the US to design the B52

00:03:38.622 --> 00:03:44.225
bomber and achieve supersonic flight. When he died, a few days after my fifth

00:03:44.225 --> 00:03:49.976
birthday, he left a 1977 E23 sedan in his Yellow Springs driveway. His glovebox

00:03:49.976 --> 00:03:55.432
contained a few tattered maps, a BMW owner’s manual, 1st and 2nd class Iron

00:03:55.432 --> 00:04:01.109
Crosses, a Front Flying Clasp, and an award from the US Department of Defense,

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:06.270
pinned to the front page of the March 26th issue of the New York Times.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:10.964
His denim blue ribbon was embroidered with white stitches running its

00:04:10.964 --> 00:04:16.142
three-inch length down to a folded triangle that held an 8mm diameter yellow

00:04:16.142 --> 00:04:21.803
metal jump ring. A small tube-shaped bail connected the loop to a soft-edged, cast,

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:27.394
octagonal bronze medal with a background filled with 13 debossed stars. The center

00:04:27.394 --> 00:04:32.503
supported a bas-relief forearm in profile starting on the bottom leg of the

00:04:32.503 --> 00:04:37.404
octagon, pointing up to a fist that closed around three arrows, pointing

00:04:37.404 --> 00:04:42.237
west. “DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE” circumscribed the front of the medal. The

00:04:42.237 --> 00:04:47.691
back showed an open-topped wreath that held the dedication “Awarded to Siegfried

00:04:47.691 --> 00:04:52.937
Knemeyer for Distinguished Civilian Service.” SK’s name was machine engraved,

00:04:52.937 --> 00:04:58.529
while the remainder of the lettering was in the wax pattern when it was burned out

00:04:58.529 --> 00:05:02.740
of the mold and filled with an orange alloy of copper and tin.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:08.231
The sketch for that medal, and for the illustration on page A11 of the issue of

00:05:08.231 --> 00:05:13.651
The New York Times it was found on, were both made on a prototype of the first

00:05:13.651 --> 00:05:18.931
consumer graphics tablet, Apple Model No. A2M0029, which was released to the

00:05:18.931 --> 00:05:24.492
general public on April 12, 1979. While the wired black stylus could be a little

00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:29.913
awkward to use, the 94 colors and 40 brushes included with the optional Utopia

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:35.122
Graphics Tablet System software allowed users to create “intricate designs,

00:05:35.122 --> 00:05:40.754
brilliant colors, and animated graphics” with ease. A fifty-year-old architect in

00:05:40.754 --> 00:05:45.752
Los Angeles took some time away from cutting and folding paper models to

00:05:45.752 --> 00:05:50.539
sketch yellow rectangles with pixelated holes on his first generation

00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:56.311
tablet—noting that the 280 by 192 picture element grid was big enough to have 18 to

00:05:56.311 --> 00:06:01.661
36 pixels per window. He imagined young men and women reading law a few miles

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:05.885
from where he studied chemical engineering and took his first

00:06:05.885 --> 00:06:11.305
architecture class, twenty-five years earlier. Maybe some of them would change

00:06:11.305 --> 00:06:16.937
their majors too. He drew staircases with pixels as steps, jutting out diagonally

00:06:16.937 --> 00:06:22.217
from the facade, with a row of jagged perpendicular cylinders. He dreamed of

00:06:22.217 --> 00:06:27.074
erecting buildings that wrote plastic software for progressive people.

00:06:27.074 --> 00:06:32.128
We started simple: cupping our hands to move water from streams to lips. We

00:06:32.128 --> 00:06:37.593
noticed puddles and ponds, extended and reduced them in size until we could carry

00:06:37.593 --> 00:06:42.647
our drinks in mugs, bags, and pots we brought from bush to cave to plain to

00:06:42.647 --> 00:06:47.565
metropolis. We needed to sort and identify these public properties, so we

00:06:47.565 --> 00:06:53.029
projected the patterns we developed for skin, wall, and cloth into decoration for

00:06:53.029 --> 00:06:58.425
hard surfaces (that we painted, hammered, and glazed as we conquered matter.) We

00:06:58.425 --> 00:07:03.753
spelled out our myths, we projected our graphic fears, and told our origin lies

00:07:03.753 --> 00:07:04.504
on objects.

00:07:04.504 --> 00:07:09.686
Over millennia, these styles became manners and consumed the vessel—becoming

00:07:09.686 --> 00:07:14.937
units of commercial trade that turned into noise that flipped into symbols of

00:07:14.937 --> 00:07:15.835
authenticity.

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:21.129
Why would you consume vastly more energy than is required to produce something?

00:07:21.129 --> 00:07:25.701
The modern handmade cup is an asynchronous glyph—a broken, orphaned

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:30.342
logo of an idioglossic dialect; a forgotten language masquerading as

00:07:30.342 --> 00:07:35.953
vernacular. This is precisely why it can be thought of as fine art, why we can map

00:07:35.953 --> 00:07:41.634
ideas into the labor and the surface that has little shared direction—because it is

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:47.037
unnecessary, extravagant, pointless. Some things are pushed from enhancement to

00:07:47.037 --> 00:07:52.440
obsolescence, which later flip back into desirable good—but they are never what

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:57.705
they were. We think of ourselves as “modern practitioners of an ancient art,”

00:07:57.705 --> 00:08:02.692
but there are no ancient arts to practice—just their archived objects and

00:08:02.692 --> 00:08:07.957
the stories we tell about them. Even if we pick up those tools and follow old

00:08:07.957 --> 00:08:13.291
orders of operation, the clients for that work are extinct. Our reverence is a

00:08:13.291 --> 00:08:18.278
codpiece, protecting our gems from freezing as we try to “step twice into

00:08:18.278 --> 00:08:19.456
the same river.”.

00:08:19.456 --> 00:08:24.723
People think a storm is coming: something big, wet and biblical. Everywhere you

00:08:24.723 --> 00:08:29.788
turn there are signs: seven spun golden candlesticks, a dude with seven sawn

00:08:29.788 --> 00:08:34.785
stars in his hand, and some confused people holding onto seven paper crowns

00:08:34.785 --> 00:08:39.849
with seven sweaty hands. People aren’t reading as much as your semi-literate

00:08:39.849 --> 00:08:45.116
grandmother remembers; they aren’t as polite as they were when they called each

00:08:45.116 --> 00:08:50.316
other faggots, broads and papists in the 1950s; and they aren’t as curious and

00:08:50.316 --> 00:08:55.650
hungry for knowledge as they were when we had those big printed encyclopedias in

00:08:55.650 --> 00:09:00.783
our studies that were rarely opened. We are coarse, having loud conversations

00:09:00.783 --> 00:09:05.644
about our relatively minor differences, and we have plenty (of booze.) So

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:09.426
obviously, it’s only a matter of time before the rapture.

00:09:09.426 --> 00:09:14.307
On August 18, 1913, the ball had fallen on black a few too many times on a

00:09:14.307 --> 00:09:19.121
roulette table at the Casino de Monte-Carlo. So people started betting on

00:09:19.121 --> 00:09:23.735
red. After 26 blacks, people kept throwing in cash as red occasionally

00:09:23.735 --> 00:09:28.415
appeared. They were expecting symmetry—waiting for a crimson flood. But

00:09:28.415 --> 00:09:33.229
the bank stuck millions of francs in their vaults, because that’s not how

00:09:33.229 --> 00:09:38.244
probability works. We deserve our gods and games, each helping us choose the

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:43.459
right wand, the right spells, and waiting for the right moment to use them. And

00:09:43.459 --> 00:09:48.675
then use them a little differently when we misjudge the moment. And then again,

00:09:48.675 --> 00:09:50.480
after a little adjustment….

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:56.530
A few months before the roulette balls fell in Monaco, a bell rang in the 300th

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:02.191
anniversary of Tsar Mikhail Romanov’s ascension to the throne of Russia. A

00:10:02.191 --> 00:10:08.241
film, commissioned by the Tercentenary Committee, showed the progeny of Michael

00:10:08.241 --> 00:10:14.523
I’s military regiments in cylindrical fur hats, parading down churchsteps into the

00:10:14.523 --> 00:10:19.952
snow, with streets full of neusurfs looking on. A camera zoomed in on a

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:26.079
vertical banner covered with a painting of each of the twenty tsars and tsarinas

00:10:26.079 --> 00:10:32.051
that owned Russia from the end of the Time of Troubles and into the world that

00:10:32.051 --> 00:10:37.636
would soon be plunged into war, 1613-1913. In front of this awkward image

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:43.065
sat a rock crystal egg, skinned in cut-ice cracks, in two hollow halves

00:10:43.065 --> 00:10:48.727
(each rimmed with diamond-studded platinum.) It was presented to the fifth

00:10:48.727 --> 00:10:54.543
richest man in the world, Tsar Nicholas II. This well-documented Easter egg,

00:10:54.543 --> 00:11:00.826
designed by Alma Pihl and constructed in the Faberge workshop (headed by her uncle

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:06.565
Albert Homstrom) contained a miniature white gold basket, filled with white

00:11:06.565 --> 00:11:12.537
quartz flowers, with yellow gold stems and stamens, along with more than 3,000

00:11:12.537 --> 00:11:17.966
diamonds. The Winter Egg cost (the profoundly anti-semitic) Nicholas II

00:11:17.966 --> 00:11:20.991
24,600 rubles and, in effect, his life.

00:11:20.991 --> 00:11:26.171
Until relatively recently, orgies of labor like this were relatively rare and

00:11:26.171 --> 00:11:31.556
connected almost exclusively to kingdoms and churches. But as the middle classes

00:11:31.556 --> 00:11:37.008
broke off from the ranks of paupers and aristocracy, their wealth began demanding

00:11:37.008 --> 00:11:41.916
effervescent baubles—things that would serve as evidence of culture. This

00:11:41.916 --> 00:11:47.096
patronage allowed increasingly diverse workshops to develop, ones that were a

00:11:47.096 --> 00:11:52.481
little more loosely knotted to the purse strings of tyrants and popes. • Look at

00:11:52.481 --> 00:11:58.002
the work of Daniel Brush. While it isn’t quite as detailed or virtuosic as some of

00:11:58.002 --> 00:12:02.909
the Faberge work, there is more independence and individual virtue in his

00:12:02.909 --> 00:12:08.157
work. It is the work of a man in a small workshop, making the things that have

00:12:08.157 --> 00:12:12.724
remained unmade for too long. He developed clients with the means to

00:12:12.724 --> 00:12:17.972
support this research. This power, to compete with the state and the church on

00:12:17.972 --> 00:12:23.493
even matters as relatively unimportant as artistic production, is a great force of

00:12:23.493 --> 00:12:28.946
populist jealousy. We want our greatest minds, money, and talents at work for the

00:12:28.946 --> 00:12:34.331
masses and the articles of their faith, not in the service of minority interests

00:12:34.331 --> 00:12:39.647
that the rest of us can’t understand or enjoy. We identify with our regents and

00:12:39.647 --> 00:12:44.964
priests, and disempowered idiosyncrasy just won’t stand. So we stand in line to

00:12:44.964 --> 00:12:48.576
see the Eggs in museums, in lust with their authority.

00:12:48.576 --> 00:12:53.633
Europe has made things difficult for Jews so long as the idea of Europe has

00:12:53.633 --> 00:12:58.416
existed, but pogroms in Russia, sanctioned by the Tsars and the Russian

00:12:58.416 --> 00:13:03.815
Orthodox church, were the standard bearer for the nineteenth century phenomenon.

00:13:03.815 --> 00:13:09.350
Jews were believed to drink the blood of Christians, specifically children. Men of

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:14.065
letters wrote, portmanteaued, and distributed variations of this blood

00:13:14.065 --> 00:13:18.985
libel through The Protocols of the Elders of Zion, using it as proof of a

00:13:18.985 --> 00:13:24.247
conspiracy that “the fundamental feelings animating the Talmudic spirit are an

00:13:24.247 --> 00:13:29.440
overweening ambition to dominate the world, an insatiable lust to possess all

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:34.497
the riches of those who are not Jewish, and a grudge against Christians and

00:13:34.497 --> 00:13:39.622
against Jesus Christ.” On October 8, Mendel Beilis went on trial, accused of

00:13:39.622 --> 00:13:45.157
killing a Christian child and baking his blood into a Passover matzo—with the full

00:13:45.157 --> 00:13:50.145
prosecutorial zealotry of the Russian empire in Kiev. The ‘Black Hundreds’

00:13:50.145 --> 00:13:55.544
passed out a leaflet that “the yids have tortured Andrusha Yushcinsky to death!”

00:13:55.544 --> 00:14:00.737
Priests, drunks, and thieves testified against Beilis, a local bricklayer. He

00:14:00.737 --> 00:14:05.931
was found not-guilty (but was not found innocent to the true believers of the

00:14:05.931 --> 00:14:11.397
libel who later called the bars rumored to be made from human tallow at Auschwitz

00:14:11.397 --> 00:14:12.354
Beilis Soap.).

00:14:12.354 --> 00:14:18.187
How can we know how much Christian blood a person-of-interest has consumed? First,

00:14:18.187 --> 00:14:23.443
we will have to differentiate between those people who were simply born to

00:14:23.443 --> 00:14:28.844
Christians, those who were baptized as Christians, and those who are leading

00:14:28.844 --> 00:14:33.596
Christian lives. Some metaforensic chemists would insist on a finer

00:14:33.596 --> 00:14:39.213
pathologic gradation, between Western and Eastern Orthodox churches, Protestant

00:14:39.213 --> 00:14:44.685
denominations, and Christian cults of the New World, but God’s soldiers don’t

00:14:44.685 --> 00:14:50.302
always have that kind of time at their gun range shopping mall. For the sake of

00:14:50.302 --> 00:14:55.487
demonstrating a basic blood libel titration workflow, at least a liter of

00:14:55.487 --> 00:15:00.815
blood must be taken from the subject, and precisely 10ml of this analyte is

00:15:00.815 --> 00:15:06.720
carefully added to an Erlenmeyer flask. A sterile serological pipette, containing a

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:12.192
PZ reagent, is slowly measured off until the analyte begins glowing gold. The

00:15:12.192 --> 00:15:17.881
volume of the reagent is measured, and a concentration calculation is performed.

00:15:17.881 --> 00:15:23.627
A concentration of more than 1000 INRI cells (tsarocytes) per five million red

00:15:23.627 --> 00:15:29.522
blood cells (erythrocytes) indicates a Christian who is likely in the midst of a

00:15:29.522 --> 00:15:35.566
crusade, with sword in hand. These people are to be given provisions and sent back

00:15:35.566 --> 00:15:41.685
to do battle with Satan and nonbelievers, statim. Measurements between 700 and 1000

00:15:41.685 --> 00:15:47.206
are the real deal; they are often wealthy heirs to industrial fortunes that

00:15:47.206 --> 00:15:52.952
underwrite missions and superPACs to promote Young Earth creation, patriarchy,

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:58.474
and other family values in public schools. Formal apologies should be given

00:15:58.474 --> 00:16:04.369
to each of these subjects accidentally caught up in the system. Tsarocyte levels

00:16:04.369 --> 00:16:10.338
between 500 and 700 are consistent with your garden variety pamphleteer, but will

00:16:10.338 --> 00:16:15.711
sometimes indicate latent rapture magnetism. Give them crackers and 300ml

00:16:15.711 --> 00:16:21.158
of purified christ serum. Counts between 300 and 500 generally make up the

00:16:21.158 --> 00:16:26.755
religious laity, but also their priests. The counts would be higher, but the

00:16:26.755 --> 00:16:32.202
ministerial class is fond of opening up their veins in front of television

00:16:32.202 --> 00:16:37.948
cameras anytime one of their flock is injured by being reprimanded for calling

00:16:37.948 --> 00:16:42.723
someone a faggot. They require no remediation; they are routinely

00:16:42.723 --> 00:16:48.544
re-infused with spirit cells every time they tell someone they are a Christian.

00:16:48.544 --> 00:16:54.140
Below 300 INRI cells, and we have a serious problem. These are either lapsed

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:59.289
Christians, those who were never baptized, people who voted for Barack

00:16:59.289 --> 00:17:05.258
Obama, or patriots whose NRA memberships have lapsed. Quarantine them and contact

00:17:05.258 --> 00:17:10.034
the Ministry of Ministries immediately to start a support ticket.

00:17:10.034 --> 00:17:15.867
Results of greatest concern, however, are the INRI3 cell counts. When a Christian

00:17:15.867 --> 00:17:21.627
is martyred, their soul is immediately pressed into action; transforming each of

00:17:21.627 --> 00:17:27.459
their tsarocyte cells into viral markers. The RNA polymerase catalyzation process

00:17:27.459 --> 00:17:32.854
is retranscribed, turning INRI1 into INRI3—recognizable by a characteristic

00:17:32.854 --> 00:17:38.760
guanine horn on each carbon3 nucleotide. A count of below 100ppm is usually caused

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:44.520
by simple cross-contamination; the blood of dead Christians that might have been

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:50.353
accidentally ingested after having been picked up on discarded weapons, or having

00:17:50.353 --> 00:17:55.894
been accidentally mixed into hamburger made from the unsaved. Between 100 and

00:17:55.894 --> 00:18:01.726
200 INRI3 cells generally indicates that there is occasional blood consumption of

00:18:01.726 --> 00:18:07.486
older Christians, probably as they prayed in nursing homes. Between 200 and 300,

00:18:07.486 --> 00:18:13.319
and you’re probably dealing with a serial ‘vampire of the righteous.’ Between 300

00:18:13.319 --> 00:18:18.568
and 400, and they have at least occasionally poured the blood of children

00:18:18.568 --> 00:18:24.109
who were ritually slaughtered while having been forced to recant the divinity

00:18:24.109 --> 00:18:29.359
of their savior. And above 400 INRI3 units indicates that the subject has

00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:35.119
recently bathed in a solution of aborted fetal tissue and holy water and may, at

00:18:35.119 --> 00:18:40.878
any moment, transform into someone who refuses to genuflect in the presence of a

00:18:40.878 --> 00:18:46.274
yellow ribbon. Any of these indications require the technician to call Kirk

00:18:46.274 --> 00:18:52.034
Cameron on his hotline at the Corporation for the Elimination of Vice within two

00:18:52.034 --> 00:18:56.991
business hours. Videotape of the immediate executions, corpses of the

00:18:56.991 --> 00:19:02.314
subjects, their personal effects, serology reports, and form 07SL, must be

00:19:02.314 --> 00:19:07.636
transferred to the local Kroc recycling center in approved Glad® bags. Any

00:19:07.636 --> 00:19:12.448
biohazardous remains can be sterilized with stale hosts and prayer.

00:19:12.448 --> 00:19:18.018
We know there is something there, but its shape is something we tend to ignore

00:19:18.018 --> 00:19:23.371
until we can feel it. Our hands are pushed back when they hang out windows,

00:19:23.371 --> 00:19:28.290
our feathers don’t fall as fast as bricks, and our engines burn as we

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:33.715
imagine breath is oxygen. Air is a wall, so we make chisels. Our screens and

00:19:33.715 --> 00:19:39.141
bullets, blades and dams, spoilers and grilles are wings; chewing up what we

00:19:39.141 --> 00:19:44.783
once thought the son of Erebus and Nyx. We suck up Aether and breathe out fiery

00:19:44.783 --> 00:19:46.953
Cinderellas, forever midnight.

00:19:46.953 --> 00:19:52.330
You can guard the eyes, the ears, or the mouth, but something is always exposed.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:56.891
Our neckrolls protected us from the hardest hits. They pumped up the

00:19:56.891 --> 00:20:02.268
silhouette of our traps, they kept the borders of our helmets from being pressed

00:20:02.268 --> 00:20:07.714
into our chests and our spines from being snapped sideways. But as we put on more

00:20:07.714 --> 00:20:12.955
gear, we took on bigger risks. The more armor, the more hubris. We rushed into

00:20:12.955 --> 00:20:18.264
battle wearing our brightwork, only to find that our enemies have been starving

00:20:18.264 --> 00:20:23.437
themselves to slip their bodies beneath our breastplates. What they lacked in

00:20:23.437 --> 00:20:28.746
muscle they’ve toned in speed—an offense at terminal velocity, twisting what we

00:20:28.746 --> 00:20:33.919
thought indomitable. For all the energy that goes into our uniforms, they are

00:20:33.919 --> 00:20:39.229
still amulets; with all the protective power of fools dumb enough to believe in

00:20:39.229 --> 00:20:39.569
them.

00:20:39.569 --> 00:20:46.060
It starts with a curve, tracing an archetypal silver stick that skins space

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:52.026
a candle never has. It is slit into style, spouts a teapot, undergoes

00:20:52.026 --> 00:20:58.780
mitosis, rises on a soft square and gives off gold while mirroring memories of

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:05.359
Myra, Teresa, Tom, Billie, Philippe, Doug, Pam, Matt, Steven, Patrick, John,

00:21:05.359 --> 00:21:09.570
Karim, Rebecca and Frankie in a mimetic universe.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:14.493
Look, swipe, sketch, edit, surface, read, flow, render, post, repeat….

00:21:14.493 --> 00:21:19.926
Edit, sketch, flow, post, render, swipe, look, surface, read, repeat….

00:21:19.926 --> 00:21:26.174
The timeless is a cliché that lends reflected images to experimenters revered

00:21:26.174 --> 00:21:32.092
for originality. The trendy are near-finities of also-mades that are easy

00:21:32.092 --> 00:21:33.161
to disregard.

00:21:33.161 --> 00:21:38.169
We don’t lose time worrying about theft, because it is so common. But the

00:21:38.169 --> 00:21:43.176
appropriation of the cult or the overlooked is the dark end of dreams. We

00:21:43.176 --> 00:21:47.836
see brilliance where there is but shadow cast beneath stolen matter.

00:21:47.836 --> 00:21:52.755
Verb is the word that takes ordinary—insert products here—and lends

00:21:52.755 --> 00:21:58.270
direction, function; makes me feel like I’m already using them and couldn’t

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.282
imagine myself still again!

00:22:00.282 --> 00:22:05.258
Disconnected thoughts seamed together—whole. Marketable, collectible,

00:22:05.258 --> 00:22:10.307
displayable, useable, modern place settings; retraining wrist postures

00:22:10.307 --> 00:22:14.771
everywhere! Curvy shapes with Palate-Scald Mitigation System®.

00:22:14.771 --> 00:22:20.879
Darting eyes examine, dissect, observe, record, and process. Poised fingers

00:22:20.879 --> 00:22:26.739
grasp, sketch, click, type, and plan. Machines slice, print, burn, cast.

00:22:26.739 --> 00:22:33.177
Blurred hands cut, file, bend, forge, refine, and atomized plastic pigments are

00:22:33.177 --> 00:22:35.901
(-) attracted, baked, and sealed.

00:22:35.901 --> 00:22:41.946
Computer assisted design, mixed media construction, hand/machine-made,

00:22:41.946 --> 00:22:47.027
non-nesting, definitely undishwasher-safe. Wrap your digits

00:22:47.027 --> 00:22:52.547
around the heat capable, corrosion-averse, cobalt stalk; squeeze

00:22:52.547 --> 00:22:59.118
the soft, palm-sized, rubber bellows (reciprocate.) Lift, dip, pierce, cool,

00:22:59.118 --> 00:23:00.607
consume, repeat….

00:23:00.607 --> 00:23:05.789
Hair is identity. Not just something in your bones, not just something you run

00:23:05.789 --> 00:23:10.769
your wet fingers through, not just something to differentiate you from your

00:23:10.769 --> 00:23:15.749
dry peers—your hair is the soul you imagine is in your chest. You can shave

00:23:15.749 --> 00:23:20.864
and color and style it, but its essence hangs on as aura. It’s waiting in you

00:23:20.864 --> 00:23:25.979
when you’re born, it’s there in pitch blackness when you’re running away from

00:23:25.979 --> 00:23:31.296
what you fear most, and it will survive the person you recognize in personality.

00:23:31.296 --> 00:23:36.545
Hair is worn down and etiolated as sheets of time twist, are snapped smooth and

00:23:36.545 --> 00:23:41.862
folded. As your body loses water, it will shrink and pull away from each strand.

00:23:41.862 --> 00:23:46.775
The white light you wander toward will be made of photons; split from your

00:23:46.775 --> 00:23:52.024
trimmings, burning at the edge of your horizon. Hair is what you tangle with in

00:23:52.024 --> 00:23:54.245
life and where you nest in death.

00:23:54.245 --> 00:23:59.638
Every single thing is placed precisely where force sent it. Gravity, friction,

00:23:59.638 --> 00:24:04.471
inertia, acceleration, thrust, drag and torque, sure; but also hatred,

00:24:04.471 --> 00:24:09.724
incompetence, will, lust, titillation, neglect and misunderstanding. Some of

00:24:09.724 --> 00:24:15.327
these are coded into things when they are born: iron will combine with oxygen and

00:24:15.327 --> 00:24:20.650
other elements, eventually wasting into fatigue and failure. It was all there

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:26.184
when the Bang cooled—in the moment it was pulled out of the Earth and smelted by

00:24:26.184 --> 00:24:31.717
our extensions. It remained when the bolt was tightened, and it will fail unless

00:24:31.717 --> 00:24:37.390
energy is expended to maintain it. We are smarter apes, in some ways, than we used

00:24:37.390 --> 00:24:42.783
to be—we alloy and coat and choose the right metal for the right job. Maybe we

00:24:42.783 --> 00:24:48.247
will eventually have to live with our mistakes for something that seems eternal

00:24:48.247 --> 00:24:53.640
to mortals, but few of our things will likely outlive our race. Things are all

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.060
waste.
